From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:33:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 089/144] remoteproc: qcom: retain the SM8750 SoCCP bootstrap
 owner

Keep a checked, bounded per-node interconnect owner across failed probes.
Serialize firmware transitions with the complete system-suspend gate and
release both bootstrap and proxy resources only after authenticated start,
ready, handover and D3, or a proven PAS shutdown.

Require built-in PAS and static DT for the new SoCCP instance. A separate
driver suppresses its bind attributes without changing other PAS devices.
Keep generic runtime nodes disabled until board firmware is supplied.

These lifetime and error-handling changes are local adaptations of the
Armada implementation and its Kettle API port, kept in separate patches.

Link: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/tree/db09dd6c6dfd134bbcf04218042bd06146ebbd8f/packages/kernel/patches
Link: https://github.com/kettlelinux/kettlelinux/tree/e9013946c87eb94052ff687a9bb5183a31b67751/kernel/patches/40-kettle
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>

